            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for to reflect on, then the Kannada for intellect."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಸಂಗತಿ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸಂಗತಿ — saṅgati — \"a fact; a matter\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಈ ಸಂಗತಿ ಯಾರಿಗೂ ಗೊತ್ತಿರಲಿಲ್ಲ. ī saṅgati yārigū gottiralilla. Nobody knew this fact."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ವಿಷಯ is a topic; ಸಂಗತಿ (saṅgati) is something that is so."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸಂಗತಿ (saṅgati) is borrowed from Sanskrit saṃgati, \"a coming together, a meeting\" (Monier-Williams); Kannada uses it for a matter or a fact."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
